  "verificationTiming": [
    "Initial 88 independent browser and 23 fixture-PDF checks preceded the legacy whole-color repair; final 20 focused color checks cover changed behavior, followed by 49 targeted checks and full complex regression.",
    "Complex initial failure exposed the real whole-color regression plus semantically equivalent missing-versus-one opacity defaults. The product regression was fixed; optional-default test comparisons were normalized without weakening zero-opacity checks.",
    "Old shape test used a wrong text-array index because one line has no text. The oracle now identifies the source object; initial failure logs are retained.",
    "The final UI-only zero-value fix adds a ninth actual UI group. Core source hashes remained unchanged. Final UI PDFs were independently re-audited; PPTX hashes still exactly match native-opened files.",
    "Final full tests and build ran serially. Production UI ran after the build. All six production PPTX downloads are byte-identical to audited dev downloads; production PDFs have identical text state, drawing state and rendered pixels."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No arbitrary-document lossless compatibility or complete editor feature parity claim.",
    "Background alpha, full theme paints, advanced text effects and SmartArt cached text alpha remain bounded or protected.",
    "Alpha-only/range edits protect complex text structures; whole-frame RGB changes preserve existing fields and links.",
    "STOP validation cells require native canvas editing even for valid input; no new general formula-validation engine.",
    "Dashed PDF text fields remain readonly because the current appearance generator cannot reproduce their border.",
    "Word whole-footer replacement still removes fields, with the existing visible warning.",
    "No new macOS/Windows package or native platform validation in this iteration."
  ],
